==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Thief Cat was a part of two other [[Cat Combo]]s: [[Cybercrimes (Removed Combo)|Cybercrimes]] and [[Get Rich (Removed Combo)|Get Rich]].
*Prior to [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]], Thief Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Thief Cat
Moves fast. Steals faster.
More money earned when defeating an enemy.</pre>
<pre>Phantom Thief Cat
Moves too fast. Still steals the same.
Has a large treasure collection now.
More money earned when defeating an enemy.</pre>
<pre>Goemon Cat
Bandit of legend, last seen in old Japan fighting
against the shogun's tyranny. Slips extra money
out of enemy pockets with area attacks.</pre>
*Phantom Thief Cat is likely a reference to [[wikipedia:Arsène Lupin|Arsène Lupin]], a fictional gentleman thief created by French author Maurice Leblanc in 1905.
*Phantom Thief Cat may also be a reference to the "phantom thief" [[wikipedia:Kaito Kuroba|Kaito Kuroba]] from the ''Magic Kaito'' series. His signature weapon is his cards as a magician. He has a card-shooting gun and he always warns people before he robs them using cards or some gimmick.
*Goemon Cat is a reference to [[wikipedia:Ishikawa Goemon|Ishikawa Goemon]], a famous Japanese bandit from the Warring States period.
**Goemon Cat may also reference [[wikipedia:Ganbare Goemon|Ganbare Goemon]], as both of them are thieves who throw [[wikipedia:Koban (coin)|koban]] to attack. They also have similar red facial markings.
*The line, "The inside of its box can't become four-dimensional," in Goemon Cat's Japanese description may be a reference to [[wikia:doraemon:Doraemon (character)|Doraemon]], who has a four-dimensional pouch that he uses to store various gadgets.
*Some of the possible [[Cat Shrine#Cat Fortune|Cat Fortunes]] are "Your love rival is... Thief Cat." and "Thief Cat is in your office right now!"

